{
  "$comment": "Contract between Tiled exports and the game. Both the runtime map registry (src/assets/maps.ts) and the build-time validator (scripts/validate-maps.mjs) read this file, so a Tiled export that drifts from it fails the build instead of rendering an empty floor.",
  "tileSize": 32,
  "layerOrder": [
    "ground",
    "ground_detail",
    "buildings",
    "sorted",
    "props_above",
    "collision",
    "fx"
  ],
  "$layerOrderComment": "The render model (ADR-125). Every map has exactly these seven layers, in this order (empty allowed): ground (roads, floors) \u00b7 ground_detail (markings, grates, baked shadows) \u00b7 buildings (wall tiles) \u00b7 sorted (the Y-sort band: an OBJECT layer of everything that stands on the ground \u2014 typed placed objects, `cutout` images with a baseY + footprint, `above` images drawn over the street) \u00b7 props_above (overhead tiles: wires, awnings, canopies, roofs) \u00b7 collision (invisible: a tile stencil, or an object layer of pixel rects for generated maps) \u00b7 fx. Plus `spawns`, an object layer of points and zones outside the draw order.",
  "$sortedComment": "sorted objects: `type` = an ObjectDef id (placed object, tiles or sprite; depth from its footprint bottom), `cutout` (properties image, baseY, footprint x/y/w/h \u2014 a static body; depth = baseY), or `above` (property image; drawn at the props_above depth, never collides). Written by scripts/import-map.mjs and generate-street-map.mjs.",
  "$collisionComment": "collision as an object layer (generated maps): rects with property kind = building | prop. Buildings cover the whole wall footprint except door gaps.",
  "$pulseLayerComment": "Optional per-map `pulseLayer`: an object layer of City Pulse slots. Every slot is a named, uniquely named object with a `type` (wall, corner, shopfront, crowd). Districts list the slots they offer under pulse_slots and the validator checks they exist.",
  "$doorComment": "Any spawn-layer object named door_* or typed `door` is a door and must be 32x48 (player height = door height, design system \u00a72). The map validator warns otherwise.",
  "$sopComment": "`sop: true` marks a map migrated to the render model: every cutout needs a footprint and legacy occluders are errors. Unmigrated maps get warnings until their A5 re-audit.",
